\n\n**Metrics:** dw_4640 (direct CV precedent — full SQL retrieved), dw_2180 & dw_1221 (2014FA library/TIP join precedents), dw_3215 (SIS_SUBJECT_CODE row-number/dense-rank precedent), dw_1165, dw_3911 (library enrollment precedents).\n\n**Concepts:** concept_subject_offering_facts (granularity/enrollment comparison matrix + decision guide), concept_department_dimension (SIS_DEPARTMENT vs STUDENT_DEPARTMENT vs SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT).\n\n**Column concepts:** column_concept_enrollment_measures (decision guide: \"enrollment of subjects within the textbook program or library reserve scope → use TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS or LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\"), column_concept_term_code, column_concept_department_name, column_concept_subject_id, column_concept_master_subject_id.\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n- Graph confirms joins: SIS_SUBJECT_CODE ↔ LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED (outgoing/incoming edge), SIS_SUBJECT_CODE → SIS_DEPARTMENT (DEPARTMENT_CODE), LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED → TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED → ACADEMIC_TERMS(_ALL).\n- dw_4640 lineage: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED ⋈ STUDENT_DEPARTMENT ON OFFER_DEPT_CODE = DEPARTMENT_CODE; CV = `STDDEV(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS)/NULLIF(AVG(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS),0)` grouped by department name — a department-level scalar attached to each detail row.\n- dw_2180/dw_1221 precedent: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED joined with TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED on TERM_CODE for term '2014FA'.\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Dimension matrix (enrollment sources):**\n| Dimension | LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED | TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED | SUBJECT_SUMMARY | SUBJECT_OFFERED(_SUMMARY) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Grain | subject/term, library-reserve scope | subject/term, textbook-program scope | subject or cluster/term | section / subject per term |\n| Enrollment col | NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS | NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS | SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER | both families |\n| COURSE_NUMBER | yes | yes | no (SUBJECT_ID) | summary has COURSE_NUMBER |\n| SUBJECT_TITLE | yes | yes | yes | yes |\n(Evidence: concept_subject_offering_facts comparisons; column_concept_enrollment_measures.)\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness:**\n- Term '2014FA' + >5 enrolled + subject title + enrolled count → LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED: SUPPORTED (hint maps \"term '2014FA'\" and \"more than 5 enrolled\" explicitly to it); SUBJECT_SUMMARY: NOT-SUPPORTED (no NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS/COURSE_NUMBER mapping in hint).\n- Subject code/desc/dept name/school name → SIS_SUBJECT_CODE: SUPPORTED (hint mapping); SIS_DEPARTMENT: SUPPORTED for the Mathematics/Course-18 anchor.\n- CV of enrolled students → TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS: SUPPORTED per hint mapping and dw_4640 precedent; LIBRARY NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS: NOT the hint-mapped CV source.\n- Row number per department name ordered by subject code → window over SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_NAME/SUBJECT_CODE: SUPPORTED.\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:** \"subjects offered in the term '2014FA'\" anchors to LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE (hint). \"Mathematics department (Course 18)\" anchors to DEPARTMENT_NAME='Mathematics' AND DEPARTMENT_CODE='18' on SIS_SUBJECT_CODE/SIS_DEPARTMENT (hint). \"coefficient of variation … of the number of enrolled students in the subjects offered by the Mathematics department\" anchors to TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS with department resolved via STUDENT_DEPARTMENT (hint join key + dw_4640 SQL). No term restriction is stated for the CV, and dw_4640's DeptVariation CTE also has no term filter → CV computed across all TIP terms for Mathematics.\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence:** CV-of-enrollment precedents: 1 (dw_4640, on TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED ⋈ STUDENT_DEPARTMENT, `STDDEV/NULLIF(AVG,0)`). 2014FA library-scope precedents: 2 (dw_2180, dw_1221). SIS_SUBJECT_CODE window precedents: 1 (dw_3215).\n\n### 4. Business Usage\nLIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED serves library-reserve enrollment questions (dw_3911, dw_1301, dw_4812); TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED serves textbook-program enrollment statistics and department-level CV (dw_4640, dw_1165); SIS_SUBJECT_CODE resolves subject-code descriptions and department/school attribution (dw_3215, dw_2335, dw_3904); SIS_DEPARTMENT/STUDENT_DEPARTMENT are the department dimensions used for name/code/school filtering in these metrics.\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\n- SIS_SUBJECT_CODE: semantic_get ✓, graph neighbors ✓\n- LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED: semantic_get ✓, graph neighbors ✓\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT: semantic_get ✓\n- TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED: semantic_get ✓\n- STUDENT_DEPARTMENT: semantic_get ✓\n- dw_4640, dw_2180, dw_3215: semantic_get (full SQL) ✓; dw_1221, dw_1165, dw_3911, dw_1301, dw_4812, dw_2335: desc-level from search ✓\n- concept_subject_offering_facts, concept_department_dimension: semantic_get / search desc ✓\n- column_concept_enrollment_measures: semantic_get ✓; column_concept_term_code, _department_name, _subject_id, _master_subject_id: search desc + graph ✓\n- mysql_query: attempted 4× — all failed with \"Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'\" (database unavailable); verification by execution was impossible, noted explicitly.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a.** Main detail: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED (TERM_CODE='2014FA', NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS>5, SUBJECT_TITLE, NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) ⋈ SIS_SUBJECT_CODE ON COURSE_NUMBER (SUBJECT_CODE, SUBJECT_CODE_DESC, DEPARTMENT_NAME, SCHOOL_NAME) ⋈ SIS_DEPARTMENT ON DEPARTMENT_CODE (Mathematics / '18' anchor). CV scalar: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED ⋈ STUDENT_DEPARTMENT, `STDDEV(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS)/AVG(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS)` for DEPARTMENT_NAME='Mathematics', cross-joined. Row number: `ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY sc.DEPARTMENT_NAME ORDER BY sc.SUBJECT_CODE)`.\n\n**6b.** CTE for the CV scalar (mirroring dw_4640's DeptVariation, minus its unstated >0 filter since this question has no \"at least one enrolled student\" clause), then the detail select with exactly 8 columns in the asked order. No rounding anywhere.\n\n**6c.** *Data*: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED carries COURSE_NUMBER (the documented cross-key to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE), TERM_CODE, SUBJECT_TITLE and NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS at subject/term grain; TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED carries the CV measure per the hint mapping. *Semantic-network*: joins edges SIS_SUBJECT_CODE↔LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED and SIS_SUBJECT_CODE→SIS_DEPARTMENT exist in the graph; column_concept_enrollment_measures' decision guide directs program-scope enrollment questions to the TIP/LIBRARY columns. *Business*: dw_4640 is an exact-shape CV precedent (STDDEV/AVG over TIP ⋈ STUDENT_DEPARTMENT per department); dw_2180/dw_1221 establish the 2014FA library-scope pattern.\n\n**6d.** Alternative: computing CV from LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED instead — rejected because the hint's column mapping explicitly assigns the CV measure to TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS and dw_4640 sets the precedent. (Execution verification was not possible due to the DB access failure.)\n\n",
